{"title":"Median of a triangle","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>median</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cevian\" title=\"Cevian\">cevian</a> of the triangle that joins one <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertex</a> to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoint</a> of the opposite side. \n</p><p>In the following figure, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is a median of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/5/ae531958c09b155c0dca21e9cd9b9bb01d391fb9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import markers; pair A, B, C, M;  A = (1, 2); B = (0, 0); C = (3, 0); M = (midpoint(B--C));  draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--M); draw(B--M, StickIntervalMarker(1)); draw(C--M, StickIntervalMarker(1));  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, E); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"182\" />\n</p><p>Each triangle has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> medians.  The medians are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Concurrent\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Concurrent\">concurrent</a> at the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centroid\" title=\"Centroid\">centroid</a>. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centroid\" title=\"Centroid\">centroid</a> divides the medians (segments) in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3714d1977e2e6fa2c03536bd04eabab371fd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> ratio.\n</p>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Stewart%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Stewart&#39;s Theorem\">Stewart's Theorem</a> applied to the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec4f3da4f422b2346efe86724c8a0aee1023fac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" />, gives the length of the median to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> equal to </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f51d165d3d525f5d9ca4dbed6f8ef7783980ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac 12 \\sqrt{2AB^2+2AC^2-BC^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"198\" height=\"37\" /></center><p> This formula is particularly useful when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d39a4406ab9a6a9f1d35009c2e18008d1888fc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAB$\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" /> is right, as by the Pythagorean Theorem we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e1966560c2d736b880d71ef78e8d4ed483b41ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=AM=CM$\" width=\"149\" height=\"13\" />. This occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919b9f77a6985e760286799909be5bfe0152f40e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median_of_a_triangle&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">Altitude</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_bisector\" title=\"Angle bisector\">Angle bisector</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mass_points\" title=\"Mass points\">Mass points</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular_bisector\" title=\"Perpendicular bisector\">Perpendicular bisector</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Median_of_a_triangle&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174512\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 77/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 301/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2375/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.610      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.610      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1888:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174512 and revision id 289869. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}